WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:04.247
This is the narrated briefing
for a companion guide in the

3
00:00:04.247 --> 00:00:08.312
Federal Modernization Workbook:
The Daily Checks on One Dashboard.

4
00:00:08.312 --> 00:00:11.987
One thing first: the guide has
been reviewed and approved.

5
00:00:11.987 --> 00:00:15.433
It answers a question the
operator runbook leaves open:

6
00:00:15.433 --> 00:00:19.701
can the operator see all of the daily
checks in one place each morning?

7
00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:24.109
Mostly yes, on one Azure Monitor workbook
in the Sentinel workspace, with a

8
00:00:24.109 --> 00:00:28.663
link out to the portal that holds the data
for the checks a workbook can't read.

9
00:00:28.663 --> 00:00:31.257
Its facts come from Microsoft Learn,

10
00:00:31.257 --> 00:00:34.801
read on November eighteenth
and nineteenth, 2026.

11
00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:38.650
We'll go in four parts:
why, what, who, and how.

12
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.325
Here's the rule the guide keeps.

13
00:00:44.325 --> 00:00:48.901
The Security Operations book says it
plainly: a dashboard is a picture of the

14
00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:51.225
evidence; what an assessor relies on is

15
00:00:51.225 --> 00:00:54.275
regenerating the numbers
from the stored records.

16
00:00:54.275 --> 00:00:57.511
The Compliance Automation
book says the same of tests:

17
00:00:57.511 --> 00:01:01.250
one that reads a dashboard tile
is a screenshot with a schedule.

18
00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:03.763
So the workbook in this guide is a view.

19
00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:09.226
Every tab says so, and the kit refuses
to record a rendered view as evidence.

20
00:01:09.226 --> 00:01:12.031
The evidence stays where it already lives:

21
00:01:12.031 --> 00:01:16.560
in the record each check writes,
and the task each finding opens.

22
00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.635
What does Azure offer?

23
00:01:21.635 --> 00:01:24.260
Microsoft's guidance compares the options.

24
00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:29.210
Workbooks are a flexible canvas over the
most complete set of Azure data sources,

25
00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:32.535
and they can be managed as
Resource Manager templates.

26
00:01:32.535 --> 00:01:37.123
Portal dashboards give a single pane
of glass, but a workbook is richer.

27
00:01:37.123 --> 00:01:41.990
Dashboards with Grafana is a free
preview; Azure Managed Grafana is for

28
00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:47.023
external sources and private networking;
Power BI suits long-term trends.

29
00:01:47.023 --> 00:01:50.501
Microsoft 365 has no
single custom dashboard:

30
00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:53.797
each admin center has
its own built-in views.

31
00:01:53.797 --> 00:01:56.881
So the design is one workbook
in the Sentinel workspace,

32
00:01:56.881 --> 00:01:59.730
and a link out where the
data stays elsewhere.

33
00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.505
Here are the twelve tabs,
one per daily check.

34
00:02:06.505 --> 00:02:11.318
Telemetry completeness, the synchronization
probe, risky users and sign-ins,

35
00:02:11.318 --> 00:02:15.304
and emergency access sign-ins fit
strongly; the sync tab now also

36
00:02:15.304 --> 00:02:19.817
shows the synchronization servers'
own errors and their nightly backup.

37
00:02:19.817 --> 00:02:25.379
The new Active Directory tab, noncompliant
devices and D L P alerts fit well.

38
00:02:25.379 --> 00:02:29.952
Grants, the new admin changes tab
and the log review queue are partial:

39
00:02:29.952 --> 00:02:33.561
matching each change to a ticket
stays in the I T S M tool,

40
00:02:33.561 --> 00:02:36.368
and the review stays a recorded procedure.

41
00:02:36.368 --> 00:02:40.818
Entra Health is a link-out, because
its alerts aren't in Log Analytics.

42
00:02:40.818 --> 00:02:45.868
And the catalog tasks live in the
I T S M tool's own dashboards.

43
00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:47.759
Each server has its own row,

44
00:02:47.759 --> 00:02:52.500
so one that stops sending shows
as stale, never as a quiet night.

45
00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:58.438
What's available in G C C?

46
00:02:58.438 --> 00:03:04.084
G C C Moderate uses the commercial Entra
service and pairs with commercial Azure, so

47
00:03:04.084 --> 00:03:09.650
the workspace, the workbook and the Logs
Ingestion API are all in commercial Azure.

48
00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:13.801
Entra and Intune both send
their logs to the workspace;

49
00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:16.937
Intune in G C C is the
commercial instance.

50
00:03:16.937 --> 00:03:22.113
Defender X D R alerts and incidents
are generally available for G C C.

51
00:03:22.113 --> 00:03:24.824
The Defender portal's
connector overview is a

52
00:03:24.824 --> 00:03:27.463
commercial-cloud preview,
so it isn't assumed.

53
00:03:27.463 --> 00:03:29.704
For the servers that stay on premises,

54
00:03:29.704 --> 00:03:32.525
the Azure Monitor Agent
on Arc-enabled servers,

55
00:03:32.525 --> 00:03:37.805
the Windows security events connector and
the Azure activity connector are available

56
00:03:37.805 --> 00:03:41.060
in commercial Azure, and
Defender for Identity alerts

57
00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:44.387
are generally available for G
C C, with their own license.

58
00:03:44.387 --> 00:03:47.781
And Entra Health monitoring
and Connect Health,

59
00:03:47.781 --> 00:03:52.640
for sync and for A D D S, are not yet
specified, so their tabs link out.

60
00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:57.315
Who does what?

61
00:03:57.315 --> 00:04:00.305
Security operations is
accountable for the sources,

62
00:04:00.305 --> 00:04:04.315
the template and the deployment, and
for the telemetry tab each morning.

63
00:04:04.315 --> 00:04:08.300
Identity engineering connects
the Entra logs and the probe,

64
00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:11.328
and supplies the emergency
access object I D's.

65
00:04:11.328 --> 00:04:16.490
The endpoint platform owner connects Intune
and supplies the compliance state value.

66
00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:19.378
The operators read
their own family's tabs.

67
00:04:19.378 --> 00:04:22.408
And the security officer
is consulted on each plan,

68
00:04:22.408 --> 00:04:27.310
approving its hash in the change record,
and is accountable for the evidence.

69
00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.372
Now the six steps.

70
00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:34.585
Step 1 connects the sources.

71
00:04:34.585 --> 00:04:39.848
An Entra diagnostic setting sends sign-in,
audit and risk logs to the workspace.

72
00:04:39.848 --> 00:04:43.683
Intune's diagnostic settings
send the compliance export,

73
00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:46.160
once a day, up to forty-eight hours late.

74
00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:49.801
The Defender X D R connector
brings incidents and alerts,

75
00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:52.744
including those it collects
from Purview D L P.

76
00:04:52.744 --> 00:04:55.610
Health monitoring is
turned on for Sentinel.

77
00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:59.808
And the morning synchronization
probe gets its own custom table,

78
00:04:59.808 --> 00:05:02.373
written through the Logs Ingestion API.

79
00:05:02.373 --> 00:05:05.704
The check: a read-only
reachability test reports

80
00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:08.890
each table as delivering, late or missing.

81
00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:17.452
Step 1 has three more sources, added
for the servers that stay on premises.

82
00:05:17.452 --> 00:05:21.476
The synchronization servers and
domain controllers are Arc-enabled,

83
00:05:21.476 --> 00:05:26.264
and the Azure Monitor Agent sends their
event logs and a heartbeat to the workspace.

84
00:05:26.264 --> 00:05:30.565
That replaces any script that
copies event logs to a file share.

85
00:05:30.565 --> 00:05:32.957
The domain controllers' security events go

86
00:05:32.957 --> 00:05:35.615
through the Windows
security events connector.

87
00:05:35.615 --> 00:05:41.140
A replication probe sends one record per
replication link to its own custom table.

88
00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:44.688
And the subscription's activity
log goes to the workspace,

89
00:05:44.688 --> 00:05:46.240
for the admin changes tab.

90
00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:49.042
One right in the access request is Tier 0:

91
00:05:49.042 --> 00:05:55.072
reading replication forest-wide needs
Enterprise Admins or equivalent, so the probe

92
00:05:55.072 --> 00:06:00.600
runs only on a Tier 0 host, and the Tier
0 owner decides whether it runs at all.

93
00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:07.251
Step 2 fills one settings
file per environment,

94
00:06:07.251 --> 00:06:09.854
and checks the two values
the kit can't know:

95
00:06:09.854 --> 00:06:14.838
the compliance state your workspace records,
and the product names of D L P alerts.

96
00:06:14.838 --> 00:06:16.566
Those values, and every I D,

97
00:06:16.566 --> 00:06:21.175
go into the deployed workbook's
parameters, never into the template.

98
00:06:21.175 --> 00:06:25.244
Then the validator runs ten checks on
the template, which matters because

99
00:06:25.244 --> 00:06:29.913
Microsoft says an exported template embeds
sensitive values that should be masked.

100
00:06:29.913 --> 00:06:33.264
Step 3 plans the deployment
of one workbook resource

101
00:06:33.264 --> 00:06:36.463
and previews it with what-if,
which changes nothing.

102
00:06:36.463 --> 00:06:38.955
A second person approves the plan's hash,

103
00:06:38.955 --> 00:06:42.180
and the kit refuses any
plan that would delete.

104
00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:47.293
Step 4 deploys.

105
00:06:47.293 --> 00:06:51.650
Saving a shared workbook needs the
workbooks write permission, which Workbook

106
00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:54.027
Contributor grants, and deploying through

107
00:06:54.027 --> 00:06:56.668
Resource Manager also
needs deployment rights.

108
00:06:56.668 --> 00:07:00.967
Grant both on the workbook's resource
group only, for the deployment window.

109
00:07:00.967 --> 00:07:04.631
Readers need Workbook Reader and
their own access to the data.

110
00:07:04.631 --> 00:07:07.733
The test stage runs preflight,
plans with what-if,

111
00:07:07.733 --> 00:07:11.068
deploys the approved plan,
and checks reachability.

112
00:07:11.068 --> 00:07:14.193
It's a go when each of those
has a passing live record.

113
00:07:14.193 --> 00:07:16.329
Production runs the same commands,

114
00:07:16.329 --> 00:07:20.455
and the preflight refuses it until
the test stage's evidence passes.

115
00:07:20.455 --> 00:07:23.020
Rolling back deletes a view only.

116
00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:28.808
Step 5 is the morning read.

117
00:07:28.808 --> 00:07:31.296
Telemetry completeness comes first,

118
00:07:31.296 --> 00:07:35.070
because a dark source makes
every tab over it unreliable.

119
00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:39.327
Then each tab in turn: each
row that needs work becomes,

120
00:07:39.327 --> 00:07:42.132
or is matched to, a task with an owner.

121
00:07:42.132 --> 00:07:46.032
Entra Health and the I T S M
queue are worked where they live.

122
00:07:46.032 --> 00:07:51.019
The workbook never closes a task, pages
anyone, or proves a check happened.

123
00:07:51.019 --> 00:07:56.018
Step 6 keeps the evidence: the kit
records the validation, preflight, plan,

124
00:07:56.018 --> 00:08:01.182
deployment, reachability check and
rollback plan, each hashed and chained.

125
00:08:01.182 --> 00:08:03.457
A rendered view is never recorded.

126
00:08:03.457 --> 00:08:06.010
And a portal edit comes back as an export,

127
00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:09.930
is validated, and replaces
the template through review.

128
00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:17.545
The workbook supports the monitoring
the daily checks already do;

129
00:08:17.545 --> 00:08:18.880
it doesn't add a control.

130
00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:23.241
Its records support configuration and
change control for the template and the

131
00:08:23.241 --> 00:08:25.619
deployment, and continuous monitoring for

132
00:08:25.619 --> 00:08:28.130
the reachability check;
the assessor decides.

133
00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:31.123
The biggest dangers are a
dashboard taken as evidence,

134
00:08:31.123 --> 00:08:33.518
and a missing connector
that looks healthy.

135
00:08:33.518 --> 00:08:37.917
The guards are the banner, the refused
render, and stale shown as stale.

136
00:08:37.917 --> 00:08:40.811
A silent server must
never read as a quiet one,

137
00:08:40.811 --> 00:08:44.330
and the replication probe
never runs from a lower tier.

138
00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:47.557
Some things couldn't be
verified on Microsoft Learn:

139
00:08:47.557 --> 00:08:50.109
the workbook's item format field by field,

140
00:08:50.109 --> 00:08:52.586
G C C for Entra Health and Connect Health,

141
00:08:52.586 --> 00:08:56.489
the synchronization service's
event I D's, a right narrower than

142
00:08:56.489 --> 00:09:01.142
Enterprise Admins for the probe, and
the values your own workspace records.

143
00:09:01.142 --> 00:09:04.460
The developer workbook and the
learning path take it from here.
